{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu21aTM2ARKN7mXQayXx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Password reset review: fix Step 3 first\n\n**Fix first: Step 3, the login wall.** A user who forgot their password is asked to log in before they can reset it. That's a dead end, so the flow fails at that step for its main users. It's probably the biggest cause of the support calls. Fixing it would also make Steps 1 and 4 matter, because right now few people get that far.\n\n**What to do in the sprint:**\n- Make the emailed link open the app on the reset screen, with the mobile web page as a fallback.\n- Replace the login requirement with a check that works without the password, such as a one-time code sent to the registered phone or confirmation on a trusted device.\n- Talk to security and compliance on day one. The login step may have been added on purpose as a second factor. They need to approve the replacement check, and that approval is the main risk to finishing in one sprint.\n\n**If there's time left, do these cheap fixes:**\n- **Step 4:** Show the password rules before the user types, with a live checklist. Give a specific error, such as \"Can't reuse one of your last 5 passwords.\" This is about a day of work.\n- **Step 1:** Move \"Forgot password\" next to the password field so it's visible on small screens. This is under a day.\n\n**Leave Step 2 as it is.** The neutral message stops people from using the form to check which emails have accounts, which a bank should do. You could add \"Check your spam folder\" and a resend timer.\n\n**Check before committing:** I'm inferring that Step 3 drives most of the calls. Confirm it with support call tags or a funnel showing where people drop off between link clicked and reset completed. After launch, track how often resets complete and how many reset calls support gets."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3191,"cache_read_input_tokens":5101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3191},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b3036c8-7ad2-4eac-95f5-cea49de29ab7","uuid":"7623f874-2f96-4df1-9dcc-5b87efa1d66f","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:19:43.411Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu21aECzrnWDinmz6hWV"}
